## Headline findings

**Two bugs root-caused in source**, not just observed:

1. **`write({parentId})` silently drops `layoutSizing*: "FILL"`** (new `[BUG-022]`, P1). `create.js:386` — the "apply FILL after append" pass is gated on `parentNode`, the *in-tree* parent, which is only set for children inside the same `write` tree. Attaching to an existing node via `parentId` (resolved separately as `targetParent` at `create.js:215–227`) skips it entirely. Three creates each emitted a `fill_not_applied` warning whose stated fix — "ensure parent has layoutMode" — was **wrong**; the parent already had horizontal auto-layout. Fix: `parentNode || node.parent`.

2. **`screenshot` `-32602` root cause found** (`[BUG-016]`, escalated **P1 → P0**, 4th session). `export.ts:98–113` builds `{ type: "image", data: result.imageData }` with no check that `imageData` exists — an undefined value produces a content block that's neither valid `text` nor `image`, so the SDK rejects the whole result. That's exactly the observed `invalid_union`. Two adjacent holes in the same file: the catch block omits `isError: true`, and the batch path only flags zero images as an error when `errors` is *also* populated — which is why call 6 returned `Exported 0 node(s): none` with `is_error: false`.

**Recurrences:** `[TOOL-024]` (`get_design_system` blind to library-only files) escalated **P1 → P0** — three more empty `{"variables":[],"collections":[]}` responses, the same progressive-filter-loosening dead end as session 40, in the same file 13 minutes later.

**Also new:** `[TOOL-026]` `get_enabled_library_variables` needs a query array (4 calls → 1, and it echoes 11 empty collections per response); `[TOOL-027]` `edit` exposes no `layoutPositioning`/`clipsContent`, forcing `run_script` for the connection handles — second consecutive session where pure property-setting fell to a script.

**What worked:** near-optimal `edit` batching (19 node-ops in 4 calls), the code-read sub-agent running in parallel with all Figma reads, and the `scope_mismatch` pre-check catching a fill-scoped token bound to a stroke — the agent adapted in one turn with no retry.

Tracker, metrics table, and manifest updated (sessions analyzed: 41; 14 Figma sessions remain unanalyzed). No fix plans were generated — none of the three new issues match the Phase 6 allowlist (sync-to-async / type-coercion / missing-batch-tool), so each entry carries the pinned file:line and old→new instead. `[BUG-022]` and `[BUG-016]` are both small, verified, and precisely located if you want plan files for them.
