## Session 42 — dispatching a false-positive cohort

The 11 oldest "Figma sessions" in the queue turned out to contain **no Figma work at all**. They're from an unrelated `~/Github/archivist` project, and nine of the thirteen Figmagent calls across them literally read `run_script {code: "return \"not applicable\";"}` / `"placeholder"` / `"not a figma task"` — connectivity probes, all correctly rejected with `No Figma file selected`.

I collapsed them into one document rather than generating 11 near-empty analyses, and filed the real finding as **`[INFRA-005]`** (P1): `refresh-manifest.ts` classifies a session as `figma` on ≥1 Figmagent call, which can't distinguish design work from a no-op probe. Because the queue is chronological, these sat *ahead of* the three substantive sessions — under the nightly loop they'd have burned 11 full analysis runs.

## Session 43 — `087bd997`, vip-workflows, 313 calls

A code-led session that used Figma read-only as the spec of record. That isolated the verify path, and it failed hard.

**`[BUG-016]` recurred for the 5th time — and this session falsifies the standing hypothesis.** The tracker attributed it to "larger/complex nodes." Here it fired on a **261×202 frame with 11 descendants** at `scale: 4`. The real variable is raster payload size, and the source confirms it: `document.js:609` defines `EXPORT_MAX_PAYLOAD_CHARS` with a comment stating the cap exists *because* `use_figma` does `JSON.stringify` with no size guard — but that cap is applied **only in the batch path**. `exportSingleNode` (`document.js:626–651`) has no cap at all, so `export.ts:105–112` emits `{type:"image", data: undefined}` → `invalid_union`. This reconciles every prior data point: batch is capped and survives, single is uncapped and fails past a threshold.

Two things worth your attention beyond the root cause:

- **Recovery cost was the worst on record**: 17 calls and ~8 minutes. The agent spent a `ToolSearch` locating the *competing* tool, then made 4 `mcp__plugin_figma_figma__get_screenshot` calls with `curl`+`Read` round trips each. This is the benchmark risk made concrete — it's the one failure that makes an agent abandon Figmagent mid-task.
- **`format: "SVG"` is a verified workaround** — two batch SVG calls succeeded on the same file and nodes two minutes later. That's a zero-code mitigation you could ship in the tool description today.

Also new: **`[TOOL-028]`** (P2) — those SVG exports came back as 182–707 byte *text* files emitted as binary image blobs, forcing two `Bash cat` calls to read them. Same file as the `[BUG-016]` fix; worth doing in one pass, since it turns the workaround from "usable after a cat" into "usable directly."

**`[BUG-014]`** hit its 4th onboarding occurrence (`read` before `use_file` on remote, URL in hand the whole time). And `[BUG-020]` gained confirming evidence: passing the URL as `channel:` worked first try, so the session-40 failure was purely the parameter *name*, not the value — favoring accepting `url` as an alias over renaming.

